<title>UK: BTI sets warrants on four Commonwealth currencies.</title>
<headline>BTI sets warrants on four Commonwealth currencies.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankers Trust International said it has issued 500,000 range warrants on four commonwealth currencies exchange rates against the U.S. dollars.</p>
<p>The currency pairs include the Australian dollar/U.S. dollar, the New Zealand dollar/U.S. dollar, the Canadian dollar/U.S. dollar and sterling/U.S. dollar.</p>
<p>* * * * * * *</p>
<p>CURRENCY	   SPOT	 RANGE</p>
<p>A$/US$	     0.7505     0.7295-0.7715</p>
<p>NZ$/US$	    0.6865     0.6700-0.7030</p>
<p>C$/US$	     1.3919     1.3675-1.4163</p>
<p>STG/US$	    1.6636     1.6137-1.7135</p>
<p>* * * * * * *</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE     $1.20 - 1.2 PCT OF NOTIONAL VALUE PER WARRANT</p>
<p>				 OF $100.</p>
<p> EXERCISE DATE   25.SEP.97		 PAYDATE	09.JUL.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   LUXEMBOURG</p>
<p> VALUATION	 $1.0 OR 1.0 PCT FOR EVERY URRENCY PAIR THAT</p>
<p>		     HAS TRADED WITHIN ITS RANGE AT ALL TIMES.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
